   "worked_solution": [
      {
         "step": 1,
         "text": "Substituting x = 3 gives 9 - 3 - 6 = 0 in the numerator and 9 - 9 = 0 in the denominator, so the quotient is the indeterminate form zero over zero and must be rewritten.",
         "mathjson": 0
      },
      {
         "step": 2,
         "text": "Factor both parts: x^2 - x - 6 = (x - 3)(x + 2) and x^2 - 9 = (x - 3)(x + 3). For x not equal to 3 the common factor x - 3 divides out, leaving (x + 2)/(x + 3).",
         "mathjson": [
            "Divide",
            [
               "Add",
               "x",
               2
            ],
            [
               "Add",
               "x",
               3
            ]
         ]
      },
      {
         "step": 3,
         "text": "The simplified quotient is continuous at 3, so the limit is (3 + 2)/(3 + 3) = 5/6.",
         "mathjson": [
            "Rational",
            5,
            6
         ]
      }
   ],
